    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Changing the Classification Threshold\n",
        "\n",
        "The default threshold used by `predict()` is $0.5$ for binary logistic regression. To use a different threshold, work directly with the estimated probabilities.\n",
        "\n",
        "There are three common ways to choose a threshold:\n",
        "\n",
        "- choose it manually based on the desired precision-recall tradeoff;\n",
        "- tune it on validation data or by cross-validation for a target metric;\n",
        "- derive it from an explicit cost function when error costs are known."
      ],
      "id": "365e4e3c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "threshold = 0.3\n",
        "pred_03 = (test_prob >= threshold).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "confusion_matrix(y_test, pred_03)"
      ],
      "id": "e7fed3f8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "A small helper function makes it easier to compare thresholds."
      ],
      "id": "2d860b24"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def classification_summary(y_true, prob, threshold=0.5):\n",
        "    pred = (prob >= threshold).astype(int)\n",
        "    TN, FP, FN, TP = confusion_matrix(y_true, pred).ravel()\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"threshold\": threshold,\n",
        "        \"TP\": TP,\n",
        "        \"FP\": FP,\n",
        "        \"FN\": FN,\n",
        "        \"TN\": TN,\n",
        "        \"accuracy\": accuracy_score(y_true, pred),\n",
        "        \"precision\": precision_score(y_true, pred, zero_division=0),\n",
        "        \"recall\": recall_score(y_true, pred, zero_division=0),\n",
        "        \"f1\": f1_score(y_true, pred, zero_division=0),\n",
        "    }"
      ],
      "id": "594f65bb",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "For illustration, first examine a grid of thresholds on the current evaluation data. In a real analysis, the threshold should be selected on validation data or through cross-validation, not on the final test set."
